==============================================================================
A. What does the difference diagonal MEASURE under ct-autokey?
==============================================================================
  English-in-futhorc monogram: cv over ALL 29 = 0.857   cv over nonzero 28 = 0.863
  -> ct-autokey over ENGLISH would show diagonal cv ~ 0.86. The repo's 'cv~1.0' figure is CORRECT for English plaintext.

  REAL LP2 difference diagonals: P(d=0) = 0.664%  (uniform would be 3.448%)   cv over nonzero 28 = 0.0567

  Now: ct-autokey where the PLAINTEXT is a flat, near-doublet-free stream
  (i.e. NOT English -- a key block, base-29 digits, compressed/enciphered data):
    plaintext P(rune 0)=0.00664: diagonal cv_nz = 0.0443 +/- 0.0053   P(d=0) = 0.676%
    REAL LP2:                    diagonal cv_nz = 0.0567                       P(d=0) = 0.664%

  VERDICT on the autokey refutation: the test is SOUND but CONDITIONAL.
  It refutes ciphertext-autokey-over-ENGLISH-plaintext. It does not touch
  ciphertext-autokey over a flat non-English plaintext, which reproduces the
  observed diagonal EXACTLY -- because under ct-autokey the diagonal IS the
  plaintext monogram, so a flat diagonal is a statement about the PLAINTEXT.

